{"results":[{"url":"https://www.grammar.com/grammar-check","final_url":"https://www.grammar.com/grammar-check","title":"Free Grammar Check","description":"Free grammar &#38; spell checker by Grammar.com -- check it out...","language":"en","text":"## Check your writing\n\nSpelling\n Grammar\n Clarity\n\nPaste or type your text, then select **Check my writing**. Click a highlighted phrase to review the suggested correction.\n\n## Did you know?\n\n\"I am.\" is the shortest two words sentence in the English language.\n\n---\n\nClick for more interesting facts »\n\n## Word of the Day »\n\nWould you like us to email your inbox a **FREE** new word definition every day?\n\n---\n\n#### Share your thoughts about Grammar.com with the community:\n\n* barbaraw.17454\n\n  Grammar.com was very helpful\n\n  LikeReply2 months ago\n* christinah\\_d\n\n  Hi Gath there are people working in my house they didn't finish yesterday and there is no one to check on them ,can I please work from home or submit 1 day leave\n\n  LikeReply3 months ago\n* mrw.00221\n\n  With TAROT JABI love spell. I got my lost wife and kids back with third partner gone and things are falling to place for my family. With psychicjabipowers @ gmail . com\n\n  LikeReply3 months ago\n* saulg.15406\n\n  Is it Who is prostituting now. Or is it Whom is prostituting now.??\n\n  LikeReply4 months ago\n\n  + Thelanotmyrealname\n\n    Every entry excepts evenly equal “e”.\n\n    LikeReply2 months ago\n  + heatherj.02473\n\n    Who is. Whom is only used after a preposition. For example: To Whomever is on call, ..... vs To the person who is on call, ....\n\n    LikeReply2 months ago\n* sheilaf.44133\n\n  Isn't there something slightly off about this sentence \"My exam checked out perfectly\"\n\n  LikeReply 15 months ago\n* natnael\\_s\n\n  My spring break was a refreshing mix of relaxation and productivity, allowing me to fully recharge for the final stretch of the school year.\n\n  LikeReply 16 months ago\n* williamr.86616\n\n  A wonderful concept.\n\n  LikeReply 211 months ago\n* gibin\n\n  I think that \"I can't make her sick, either.\" is correct.\n\n  LikeReply11 months ago\n* TheGroup\n\n  I just used this to correct my writing for my horror novel, I'm horrible at grammar\n\n  LikeReply 41 year ago\n\n  + BreeM\\_8998\n\n    How are your horror novels going??? I just love horror novels and find it very entertaining and am interested to hear an update about your writing if that’s okay!???\n\n    LikeReply2 months ago\n* heatherg.40120\n\n  It helped me make my poem better.\n\n  LikeReply 11 year ago\n* james.bnlc\n\n  Tired of trying to believe\n\n  LikeReply 31 year ago\n* SaketNaturopath\n\n  redefine pathology\n\n  LikeReply 11 year ago\n* pradeeplnt\\_k\n\n  Nice work guys\n\n  LikeReply 11 year ago\n* loril.74843\n\n  It gives me peace of mind knowing that grammar will be precise.\n\n  LikeReply 22 years ago\n* Cheza\n\n  Which is correct :\\_ She said, \"when?\"  \n  She said. \"When?\"  \n  She said. \"When?\"\n\n  LikeReply 12 years ago\n* mahmoudazimi\n\n  I express my deep gratitude to the developers of the Grammar site for creating such a valuable resource. This platform is highly beneficial for conducting translations and particularly for editing English documents. more »\n\n  LikeReply 32 years ago\n* williamg.41930\n\n  From your advertisement.  \n   AI assistance for any writing challenge Try It for Free  \n  For free\" is grammatically incorrect because \"free\" is not a noun, and this means it cannot be preceded by \"for\" (a preposition). In their view, something is \"sold for nothing\" or is \"sold free.\" more »\n\n  LikeReply 32 years ago\n* tameria\\_b\n\n  If we're going down to the creak today, what shoes should I bring?\n\n  LikeReply2 years ago\n* whiliana\\_a\n\n  Heart shouldn't go to school Because she is late\n\n  LikeReply 13 years ago\n* deepika\\_1\n\n  i want to ask querstion answer\n\n  LikeReply 13 years ago\n* GIZZSSY\n\n  a day dreamer\n\n  LikeReply 13 years ago\n* karag.31396\n\n  im so cunfused\n\n  LikeReply3 years ago\n* Shaza\\_719\n\n  I'm thinking for doing this as a profession but my mum don't like it\n\n  LikeReply3 years ago\n* KJB\n\n  Is the comma needed here?  \n  \"Floyd, sent me this letter.\"\n\n  LikeReply 13 years ago\n\n  + harold\\_o\n\n    :No.\n\n    LikeReply 13 years ago\n* Mrs.Murph\n\n  I have a nephew named Miles. When I write to my niece, should I ask if Miles's birthday is Friday, or if Miles' birthday is Friday?\n\n  LikeReply 13 years ago\n\n  + Sings\n\n    It makes more sense to me to write Miles' but I suspect either would be acceptable. To hear someone speak an extra 's' sound makes me cringe as well.\n\n    LikeReply3 years ago\n* BellaLittle\n\n  I am editing a book for English as a second language students. I have just come across this sentence:  \n  What does the writer say in his book?  \n  Surely this should be:  \n  What did the writer say in his book?  \n  Help please. more »\n\n  LikeReply3 years ago\n\n  + Sings\n\n    My impulse would be to ask: What is the writer saying in his book?\n\n    LikeReply 13 years ago\n* carolynt.25716\n\n  My niece always loved the American girl dolls but never had one. As a gift when she graduated from college I gave her a doll and I wrote this poem to go along with it. She loved it!\n\n  LikeReply3 years ago\n\n  + man\\_t\n\n    ..\n\n    LikeReply3 years ago\n* Sings\n\n  I frequently see statements like this and the it just sounds wrong to me. \"The dog was unable to be saved from the fire.\" Here I'm told it is correct. Wouldn't it be better to write. \"The firefighters were unable to save the dog.\" ? more »\n\n  LikeReply 13 years ago\n\n  + joanna\\_s\n\n    they're both correct, but the second form is better writing.\n\n    LikeReply 23 years ago\n* bong\\_y\n\n  I shouldn't walk fast too much.\n\n  LikeReply4 years ago\n\n  + joanna\\_s\n\n    I shouldn't walk fast too often. (I believe that's what you meant.)\n\n    LikeReply3 years ago\n* AZGail\n\n  I posted the following sentences:   \n  \"Driver's follow posted speed limits.\"  \n  \"Drivers follow posted speed limits.\"  \n    \n  They can't both be correct, folks! I say the apostrophe is an error. What say you? more »\n\n  LikeReply 14 years ago\n\n  + joanna\\_s\n\n    Drivers--if you mean more than one. The first one (Driver's) cannot be correct in the sentence as it's written.\n\n    LikeReply 13 years ago\n* Rat\n\n  Heavy rollers means, a big gambler (who spends big bucks) or a big baller.  \n  My friend said that I was a heavy roller, I asked him what did it mean. He said \"I had to have the best\" I still hadn't figured that out yet. more »\n\n  LikeReply4 years ago\n* busy\\_b\n\n  Although medieval times are well behind us, the literary greatness of Beowulf is not. Several generations have yet had the opportunity to read this timeless work. The poem proves in and of itself to be a pillar of literary excellence, its prose holds beauty in places beauty is not often seen. ----Not often seen is passive voice ---- how to change? more »\n\n  LikeReply 14 years ago\n* shavar\n\n  Can a figurtive language be used. I did not want to use leaves twice is foliage a better choice?\n\n  LikeReply4 years ago\n\n  + busy\\_b\n\n    yes it is\n\n    LikeReply4 years ago\n* busy\\_b\n\n  how can I replace passive voice? \"is seen\" ??? hurry please\n\n  LikeReply4 years ago\n* Eskridge\n\n  How to correct the spelling of a word(fault) for a mistake\n\n  LikeReply4 years ago\n* Gspu9132\n\n  Thank you all for such a memorable day. You all have given me much to hold on to but I will cherish this day forever more. As it poured down rain this evening, I couldn’t help but think…Thats Granddad, Grandma and our baby Jenny letting us know that they were there, sharing this very moment. For it is the love they shared with us that we too could share with each other. more »\n\n  LikeReply4 years ago\n* GrammerGirl\n\n  I think it's great! good job\n\n  LikeReply 14 years ago\n\n  + acronimous\n\n    Thanks!\n\n    LikeReply4 years ago\n* stever.57463\n\n  This is a great way to get your poems published, try it\n\n  LikeReply 14 years ago\n\n  + acronimous\n\n    Appreciate the good feedback -- thank you!\n\n    LikeReply4 years ago\n* shane\\_e\n\n  Awesome tool!\n\n  LikeReply 14 years ago\n\n  + acronimous\n\n    Thank you!\n\n    LikeReply4 years ago\n* shirleyo.32695\n\n  thank you!\n\n  LikeReply 14 years ago\n\n  + acronimous\n\n    It's our pleasure!\n\n    LikeReply4 years ago\n* JohnLoopstra\n\n  I write in the hope that my writing helps other people, I wish to share what I have learned in life\n\n  LikeReply4 years ago\n* jp.55104\n\n  for / birthday/ made / John/ a cake / got/ son's / his  \n  How I can organize this sentence?  \n  Thanks!\n\n  LikeReply 14 years ago\n\n  + MC27\n\n    John made a cake for his son's birthday. I hope that helps you\n\n    LikeReply 14 years ago\n* cynthias.08325\n\n  Is this sentence correct? Please tell us what topics you would like more education on?\n\n  LikeReply 24 years ago\n\n  + Soulwriter\n\n    Please tell us \\*which\\* topics.  \n    You can replace education with:  \n    Information on  \n    Instruction in\n\n    LikeReply 14 years ago\n* MammaRobin\n\n  Love the way it works, wish I could afford the premium plan, but on limited income.\n\n  LikeReply 24 years ago\n\n  + acronimous\n\n    Thank you for your kind words...\n\n    LikeReply4 years ago\n* red\\_l\n\n  Can you say \"a little instruction?\" Like in a sentence - Here's a little instruction. It doesn't feel right but I can't explain why.\n\n  LikeReply 24 years ago\n\n  + Soulwriter\n\n    Yes, you can say, 'Here's a little instruction for you' - instruction meaning general guidance, or 'Could I offer you some instruction?' - again, the word 'instruction' refers to general, not specific, guidance.  \n    If you want to refer to one or a few specific instructions, here are some alternatives:- 'Here are some pointers'  \n    - Here is a list of instructions'  \n    - 'Here's a little guidance to get you started'  \n      \n    What you say depends on what you are trying to say, to who and in what context. more »\n\n    LikeReply 14 years ago\n* Johnnywong\n\n  I am proud to use my talent to teach\n\n  LikeReply4 years ago\n* Vitaliy\n\n  Which is correct: Also I like reading books all my perfect day. or I also like reading books all my perfect day\n\n  LikeReply4 years ago\n\n  + Soulwriter\n\n    perhaps try: 'A perfect day for me, would be reading books all day.'\n\n    LikeReply 24 years ago\n* Caput\n\n  Which is correct: I wish there were a cure for all diseases or I wish there was a cure for all diseases? Why?\n\n  LikeReply 14 years ago\n\n  + TXwordie\n\n    were because it is the subjunctive.\n\n    LikeReply 14 years ago\n  + TXwordie\n\n    I wish there were a cure... you use the subjunctive tense when expressing a wish or doubt, for example; something that is not a fact.\n\n    LikeReply 14 years ago\n  + rogers\\_l\n\n    Yes, that's correct. \"Was\" doesn't belong there, simply because it's past tense.\n\n    LikeReply2 years ago\n* gandy\n\n  Which is correct?  \n  \"If there ever was someone who did not need help, it was him.\"   \n    \n  \"If there ever was someone who did not need help, it was he.\"\n\n  LikeReply 14 years ago\n\n  + Soulwriter\n\n    The former.\n\n    LikeReply4 years ago\n* Kokakola\n\n  Which one is correct, \"She has a dissent about their wedding and she dissents from/about him.\"\n\n  LikeReply 44 years ago\n* jozefm.40773\n\n  super...\n\n  LikeReply4 years ago\n* madgepat\n\n  do we say \"equal chances for\" or \"equal chances to\"\n\n  LikeReply 44 years ago\n\n  + Soulwriter\n\n    'They have an equal chance to win'. 'Is there any chance of getting a drink around here?'\n\n    LikeReply 64 years ago\n* Mesotekan\n\n  im simply asking if i should write please practice your due diligence or just practice due diligence. or is either fine?\n\n  LikeReply 55 years ago\n\n  + Soulwriter\n\n    'practice your due diligence' is correct\n\n    LikeReply 55 years ago\n* shennelle\n\n  Thank you! This is perfect, now I can see if I made any error since I have a big essay to write!\n\n  LikeReply 95 years ago\n* Belleta\n\n  This time I was in agreement with only some of the corrections.\n\n  LikeReply5 years ago\n* Belleta\n\n  Helpful.\n\n  LikeReply 25 years ago\n* quara\n\n  Fulfillment is only an outlet.  \n  Pleasure in manners of language expression not fortified as superficial, but a part of the heart.\n\n  LikeReply 15 years ago\n* Hello\n\n  Is work nicely\n\n  LikeReply 146 years ago\n\n  + rinat\n\n    Thanks for your positive feedback!\n\n    LikeReply 65 years ago\n* Linda Miller\n\n  I was pleased to have clarification on the accuracy of my writing and the spelling on a piece I submitted to Synonyms and Antonyms.\n\n  LikeReply6 years ago\n\n  + dflo\n\n    linda forgot a comma\n\n    LikeReply6 years ago\n  + dflo\n\n    and noun marker\n\n    LikeReply6 years ago\n  + dflo\n\n    to have had\n\n    LikeReply6 years ago\n  + dflo\n\n    and marker \"the\"\n\n    LikeReply6 years ago\n\n## Is this grammar correct?\n\n### Unsure how to phrase an email, document, or social post? Let our community help you get it right.\n\n---\n\n### The Web's Largest Resource for\n\n## Grammar & Spelling\n\n---\n\n### A Member Of The STANDS4 Network\n\n#### Free, no signup required:\n\n### Add to Chrome\n\nCheck your text and writing for style, spelling and grammar problems everywhere on the web!\n\n#### Free, no signup required:\n\n### Add to Firefox\n\nCheck your text and writing for style, spelling and grammar problems everywhere on the web!\n\nIt’s now more important than ever to develop a powerful writing style.\nAfter all, most communication takes place in reports, emails, and instant messages.\n\n---\n\n### Browse by letter\n\n### Quiz\n\n#### Are you a grammar master?\n\n»\n\n##### Identify the sentence with correct use of the past perfect continuous tense:\n\n**A**\nWe had eaten when she called.\n\n**B**\nI have been finished my assignment.\n\n**C**\nShe was visiting her grandparents all weekend.\n\n**D**\nThey had been working on the project for several hours before they took a break.","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":1826.498915999764,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}